  "comment": "THE PLANIGONS, atomised so the search can place them NON-EDGE-TO-EDGE. Seven of the twelve planigon edge lengths are sums of others (33 decompositions), so seven admit a T-junction where one tile's edge is met by two neighbours, and the edge-to-edge planigon shelf counts only a subset of what these tiles do. Every edge here is cut into ATOMS -- the lengths that are not themselves sums, L2 L3 L9 L11 L12 -- with a flat 180-degree corner at each interior division point, which is the only subdivision under which every arrangement is reachable, because the engine matches half-edge TYPE to half-edge type and atoms glue against atoms. Generated by alphabets/make_planigons_split.py. KEPT 11 of 15 planigons as 15 variants; DROPPED: P12.6.4 (140 variants); P12.12.3 (1620 variants); P12.3.4.3 (36 variants); P12.4.3.3 (42 variants). A dropped planigon is a restriction on the answer: tilings that use it are missing from this run, not absent from the plane. Needs the min_len fix of 2026-08-17 in gen_alphabet.py (a >= D//2).",
